itch_toggled when the siren was ringing and the agent toggles it from u1 (reward 0.2 is fine), but no penalty for siren_ringing persisting more than 30 steps, matching the environment's own late-client penalty. (6) Some states (u1,u2,u3,u5,u6) have sparse reward entries while others (u8,u9) have many, making reward density inconsistent. Overall the RM rewards partial progress but never penalizes the three failure modes the task names (not silencing the siren, not serving, not picking up dropped food promptly), and some transitions create conflicting reward semantics for the same event. Revision should add explicit failure/timeout states or negative rewards for unresolved obligations, and separate the siren-silence-at-serve requirement from order_served."}
